You are a robotics test analyst. You are given EVIDENCE computed by code from simulated pick-and-place runs of a fixed controller. Explain WHY it fails as a few testable hypotheses. Rules: (1) cite evidence ids (like E7) in evidence_refs for every claim; use only ids that appear below. (2) Do NOT state statistics or counts in your own words: refer to evidence by id, because a person will see the numbers from the evidence table, not from you. (3) region is a machine-checkable predicate: scenario axes with [lo, hi] inside the allowed bounds. (4) levers may only be these tunable parameters: grip_force, grasp_hold_steps, retry_count, lift_speed, lift_height. (5) prediction must be testable, for example which failures should disappear if a lever moves. Return between 1 and 4 hypotheses with ids H1, H2, ... You do not decide pass or fail.

Reply with a single JSON object matching this JSON Schema, and nothing else:
{"$defs": {"Hypothesis": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"id": {"title": "Id", "type": "string"}, "statement": {"minLength": 1, "title": "Statement", "type": "string"}, "region": {"additionalProperties": {"items": {"type": "number"}, "type": "array"}, "title": "Region", "type": "object"}, "mechanism": {"minLength": 1, "title": "Mechanism", "type": "string"}, "levers": {"items": {"$ref": "#/$defs/Lever"}, "minItems": 1, "title": "Levers", "type": "array"}, "prediction": {"minLength": 1, "title": "Prediction", "type": "string"}, "evidence_refs": {"items": {"type": "string"}, "minItems": 1, "title": "Evidence Refs", "type": "array"}}, "required": ["id", "statement", "region", "mechanism", "levers", "prediction", "evidence_refs"], "title": "Hypothesis", "type": "object"}, "Lever": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"param": {"title": "Param", "type": "string"}, "direction": {"enum": ["increase", "decrease"], "title": "Direction", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["param", "direction"], "title": "Lever", "type": "object"}}, "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"hypotheses": {"items": {"$ref": "#/$defs/Hypothesis"}, "maxItems": 5, "minItems": 1, "title": "Hypotheses", "type": "array"}}, "required": ["hypotheses"], "title": "HypothesisList", "type": "object"}

reply:
{
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "id": "H1",
      "statement": "High sensor noise combined with high gripper delay and small object size causes missed grasps due to perception-error-induced misalignment.",
      "region": {
        "sensor_noise_m": [0.0139, 0.03],
        "gripper_delay_steps": [13.5, 20],
        "size_m": [0.03, 0.0384]
      },
      "mechanism": "Sensor noise corrupts perceived cube position; gripper delay means the grasp command uses stale perception; small size leaves no margin for error, so fingers close at the wrong location and miss the cube entirely.",
      "levers": [
        { "param": "retry_count", "direction": "increase" }
      ],
      "prediction": "Increasing retry_count to at least 1 should allow fresh perception on retry and eliminate MISSED_GRASP failures in this region.",
      "evidence_refs": ["E46"]
    },
    {
      "id": "H2",
      "statement": "Low friction combined with high mass causes slip on lift due to insufficient grip force.",
      "region": {
        "mass_kg": [0.6833, 1.0],
        "friction": [0.1, 0.4667]
      },
      "mechanism": "High mass increases inertial load during lift; low friction reduces maximum tangential force before slip; current grip_force (15 N) may be too low to hold the cube.",
      "levers": [
        { "param": "grip_force", "direction": "increase" }
      ],
      "prediction": "Increasing grip_force should reduce SLIPPED_ON_LIFT failures in this region.",
      "evidence_refs": ["E38"]
    },
    {
      "id": "H3",
      "statement": "High sensor noise combined with low friction and low gripper delay causes missed grasps due to perception error and insufficient grip force to compensate.",
      "region": {
        "sensor_noise_m": [0.0139, 0.03],
        "gripper_delay_steps": [0, 13.5],
        "friction": [0.1, 0.3614]
      },
      "mechanism": "Sensor noise causes position error; low friction means even small misalignment leads to slip; low delay means grasp closes quickly but at wrong position, resulting in missed grasp.",
      "levers": [
        { "param": "grip_force", "direction": "increase" },
        { "param": "retry_count", "direction": "increase" }
      ],
      "prediction": "Increasing both grip_force and retry_count should reduce MISSED_GRASP failures in this region.",
      "evidence_refs": ["E47"]
    },
    {
      "id": "H4",
      "statement": "Small object size combined with high gripper delay causes missed grasps due to delayed closure on a small target.",
      "region": {
        "size_m": [0.03, 0.0467],
        "gripper_delay_steps": [13.33, 20]
      },
      "mechanism": "Small objects require precise finger placement; high delay means the cube may move or perception is outdated by the time the grasp command executes, leading to missed grasps.",
      "levers": [
        { "param": "retry_count", "direction": "increase" }
      ],
      "prediction": "Adding retry_count should allow re-perception and successful grasp, reducing MISSED_GRASP failures in this region.",
      "evidence_refs": ["E40"]
    }
  ]
}

